# Battle Arena Infra Standards

- Compose orchestration only. Sibling repos remain independent.
- Default published ports bind to localhost via per-service variables (`API_BIND_ADDRESS`, `WEB_BIND_ADDRESS`, `REALTIME_BIND_ADDRESS`, `POSTGRES_BIND_ADDRESS`, `REDIS_BIND_ADDRESS`, `MINIO_BIND_ADDRESS`). Postgres/Redis are never LAN-exposed.
- Never delete Docker volumes (e.g. `postgres_data`) without explicit approval.
- Never rotate Laravel `APP_KEY` with `--force` on startup.
- Do not hide init failures with `|| true`.
- Single environment: `docker compose up -d --build` runs the Lambda-style stack (gateway, api, console, realtime, web) plus postgres/redis/minio/mailpit. No profiles, no parallel environments.
- RustFS (S3 stand-in) always runs and stays private; avatars live there because Lambda has no persistent disk.
